/*
    UITarget.uss
    Layout for the target frame. Colours come from FishMMO-Theme.uss; the buff
    icons reuse the .buff-group classes from UIBuffContainer.uss.

    Two cards in a row: the PINNED card on the left, the HOVER card on the right.
    Each card is name and faction on one line above a health bar, then the buff
    and debuff strips. Name leads and faction trails, because faction is a
    qualifier on the name, not on the threat. C# shows and hides each card by
    whether it frames anything, so the row re-centres on one card or two.
*/

/*
    Anchored explicitly. Each panel is its own UIDocument whose root fills the
    screen, so a root with a size but no position resolves to the top-left
    corner. Top-centre, matching the uGUI target frame. The root itself paints
    nothing: it is only the row the cards sit in.

    An absolute 48px rather than 6%. An absolutely-positioned panel's containing
    block is the screen, and the screen is 1200 units wide at every aspect ratio
    but 1200 * (screenH / screenW) tall — 675 at 16:9, 800 at 1200x800. A
    percentage top therefore moves against the panels that are anchored to an
    edge in fixed units, and UIArenaHud, which sits directly under this frame,
    carries the absolute offset. These two are 48 and 132; 48 was already 6% of
    800, so nothing moved at the reference resolution.
*/
.target-panel {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 48px;
    translate: -50% 0;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    background-color: var(--clear);
}

.target-card {
    width: 260px;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding: 7px;
    margin-left: 4px;
    margin-right: 4px;
}

/*
    The pinned card is told apart by its top edge: gold instead of the panel
    brand accent, so a glance says which card is the one that will not move.
*/
.target-card--pinned {
    border-top-color: var(--gold);
}

.target-top {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.target-pin-badge {
    height: 15px;
    padding-left: 5px;
    padding-right: 5px;
    margin-right: 7px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/*
    Colour is written inline from C# — it carries the target's faction standing,
    which is a per-target fact the stylesheet cannot know.
*/
.target-name {
    flex-grow: 1;
    font-size: 12px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    -unity-text-align: middle-left;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 2px var(--edge-dark);
}

.target-faction {
    height: 15px;
    padding-left: 5px;
    padding-right: 5px;
    margin-left: 7px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.target-health {
    height: 15px;
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.target-health-fill {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 100%;
}

.target-health-text {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    font-size: 9px;
}

/*
    Buff icons the target is carrying, generated at runtime from the SERVER-filtered observed
    list. Two strips, buffs above debuffs, so a long debuff bar cannot push a defensive cooldown
    off the row the player is watching. Both reuse .buff-group from UIBuffContainer.uss.
*/
.target-buff-list {
    margin-top: 5px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.target-debuff-list {
    margin-top: 2px;
}
